A||||5||gtcash||Need better brakes||||14||
Z||000000||gtcash||05-28-2001||09:06 PM||||I would like better brakes all around...what's economical? I need to stop this 400+HP V8, 84coupe.||||reg||14
Z||000001||BV MotorSports||05-28-2001||09:22 PM||||You have many choices<P>12" Willwood (not cheap)<P>10.5 "speedway brakes" basicly s-10 4x4 rotors and front calipers and 3rd gen f-body rear calipers. You will have to pick up the adapters for the calipers and rear e-brake.<P>Grand Am brakes GA brakes and calipers at all 4 corners (loose stock e-brake) or leave the rear brakes alone to retain the e-brake.<P>All 3 you need to get an adjustable prop. valve to dail them in. I have the GA brakes at all for corners and no matter what anyone says (if done correctly with the blazer m/c) you need the prop valve to get the bias just right. Definetly so with the wieght of a v8 in back.<P>Check out: <A HREF="http://www.kitcarman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kitcarman.com</A>  ( I used his stuff) <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Brakes/Brakes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Brakes/Brakes.html</A> <BR>(nice stuff!) <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.heldmotorsports.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fierozone.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierozone.com</A> <P><BR>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtcash||05-29-2001||12:01 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by BV MotorSports:<BR>[B]You have many choices<P>12" Willwood (not cheap)<P>Wow! (not cheap) what an understatement!!!<BR>I went to their site...$2,850.00...<BR>I think I'll use the Grand Am route...<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||05-29-2001||12:08 AM||||Welcome to the board!  My advice is to Invest in Stainless braided lines to replace the rubber ones!  Cheap and effective.  I've got them on my Northstar conversion along with cross drilled rotors up front and Cadillac vented rotors and calipers at the rear.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gangster.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||05-29-2001||01:21 AM||||Forget the premade kits ..too much money.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus/fieroman/walt/walt.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus/fieroman/walt/walt.htm</A> <P>11.25" vented disc conversion ,  everything you need to know incl part #'s . I did the same conversion with Wilwood 4 piston calipers. Brakes on par with a c2 911 , grandsport vette ect. and all the parts are availavle at car quest/ autozone..<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
